@startuml i3-telephony-sequence-sip-register-invite
' I3 H2 — SIP register, then a softphone-dialled call joining the call's LiveKit room
' (docs/hld/80-telephony.md §80.2.3 flows 1, 2 and 4; D22; epics E6a (register, echo) + E6e (dial)).
'
' The deployment password comes from SIM_SIP_PASSWORD ([credential redacted]); per-user HA1 is the
' optional E6e hardening (migration 0014). No LiveKit token crosses Redis or REST towards the
' gateway: it mints its own room token like the voice agent (build_agent_token pattern).

title Softphone REGISTER + INVITE 101 → DdsCall → room join → BYE

skinparam maxMessageSize 220
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 6
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "ДДС trainee" as T
participant "Softphone\n(tools/softphone --headset\nor any SIP UA)" as SP

box "sip-gateway (profile sip)" #FFF6EF
  participant "gateway.py +\nregistrar.py + dialog.py" as GW
  participant "rtp.py + bridge.py\n(LiveKitRoomBridge)" as BR
end box

box "backend" #EFF5FF
  participant "API\napi/routers/telephony.py" as API
  participant "Use cases\nStartDdsCall, dds_call_flow" as UC
end box

box "infrastructure" #F3FFF3
  queue "Redis" as R
  database "PostgreSQL" as PG
  participant "LiveKit room\ndds-{session}-{call_id}" as ROOM
end box

participant "voice-agent" as AG

== 1. Register (E6a; Redis mirror E6e) ==

SP -> GW : REGISTER sip:<realm> (From: sip:<username>@<realm>, Expires 3600)
GW --> SP : 401 Unauthorized\nWWW-Authenticate: Digest realm, nonce, qop=auth
SP -> GW : REGISTER + Authorization: Digest (MD5)
GW -> GW : verify against SIM_SIP_PASSWORD (or users.sip_ha1, 0014)
GW -> R : SET sip:binding:{username} {contact, expires_at} EX 3600
GW --> SP : 200 OK (Contact, Expires)
note right of GW
  Wrong password ⇒ 403. Expires: 0 ⇒ unbind + DEL.
  Loss of the Redis key only makes the next click-to-call
  use the browser endpoint.
end note

== 2. The softphone dials 101 (E6e) ==

T -> SP : dial 101
SP -> GW : INVITE sip:101@<realm> + SDP offer (PCMA, PCMU, telephone-event)
GW --> SP : 100 Trying
GW -> API : POST /api/v1/telephony/dial\n{sip_user, dialed "101", sip_call_id}\n(service credential SIM_SIP_GATEWAY_SECRET)
API -> UC : dial_plan.resolve("101") → SERVICE_HEAD\nsession selection: last DDS_CARD_OPENED by this user, else oldest ACTIVE
UC -> PG : append **DDS_CALL_STARTED** {…, endpoint SIP, dialed "101",\nselection_reason LAST_OPENED_CARD}\n+ dds_calls row (DIALING)
API --> GW : 201 {call_id, session_id, room}
alt unknown number / no eligible session
  API --> GW : 404 DIAL_NUMBER_UNKNOWN / 409 NO_ACTIVE_DDS_SESSION
  GW --> SP : SIP 404 Not Found / 480 Temporarily Unavailable
end
GW --> SP : 180 Ringing
GW -> BR : allocate RTP pair (20000–20199)
BR -> ROOM : join as "sip-{call_id}" (self-minted token)
GW -> API : POST /api/v1/telephony/calls/{call_id}/leg {state UP}
API -> UC : ring [transport_ready ∧ gateway leg UP] → RINGING
UC -> R : publish voice:join {session_id, room, call_id,\ncall_kind SERVICE_HEAD, assignment_id, persona_id, endpoint SIP}
R -> AG : voice:join
AG -> ROOM : join (self-minted token)
AG -> PG : append **DDS_CALL_ANSWERED** {answered_by AI}
AG -> R : publish on session:{session_id}:events (after commit)
R -> GW : DDS_CALL_ANSWERED (gateway subscribes for bridged calls)
GW --> SP : 200 OK + SDP answer (PCMA, ptime 20)
SP -> GW : ACK

== 3. Media ==

SP <-> BR : RTP G.711 8 kHz, 20 ms frames
BR <-> ROOM : audioop ratecv 8k ↔ 48k; publish mic track / play the agent's track
ROOM <-> AG : LiveKitCallTransport (unchanged): first remote audio track = the gateway's

== 4. Hang-up from the softphone ==

T -> SP : hang up
SP -> GW : BYE
GW --> SP : 200 OK
GW -> API : POST /api/v1/telephony/calls/{call_id}/leg {state DOWN}
API -> UC : hang_up / TRAINEE
UC -> PG : append **DDS_CALL_ENDED** {reason HANGUP, duration_ms}
UC -> R : publish voice:cancel:{session_id} {call_id, reason HANGUP}
R -> AG : leave the room
BR -> ROOM : leave

note over GW, ROOM
  Echo extension 999 (E6a) never reaches the backend or a room: rtp.py sends the
  payload back — the interop and latency probe (benchmark_voip.py --path sip-loopback).
  A hang-up from the browser or the backend arrives as voice:cancel:{session_id};
  the gateway then sends BYE to the softphone.
end note

@enduml
